:"stringdb::description","v":"Glutamate receptor 1; Ionotropic glutamate receptor. L-glutamate acts as an excitatory neurotransmitter at many synapses in the central nervous system. Binding of the excitatory neurotransmitter L-glutamate induces a conformation change, leading to the opening of the cation channel, and thereby converts the chemical signal to an electrical impulse. The receptor then desensitizes rapidly and enters a transient inactive state, characterized by the presence of bound agonist. In the presence of CACNG4 or CACNG7 or CACNG8, shows resensitization which is characterized by a delayed accumulati [...] "},{"po":110196,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"1.409216","d":"double"},{"po":110196,"n":"display name","v":"GRIA1"},{"po":110196,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.048227","d":"double"},{"po":110196,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"-0.5809445262839944","d":"double"},{"po":110196,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":110196,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"1.599034","d":"double"},{"po":110196,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(255,0,0)"},{"po":110196,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000428994"},{"po":110196,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"2.286842","d":"double"},{"po":110196,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"1.598926","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":110193,"n":"compartment::golgi apparatus","v":"1.595939","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"3.898966","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["2h9r_C","5nin_C","AF-P24588"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":110193,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"0.684102","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":110193,"n":"tissue::liver","v":"1.354642","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"compartment::extracellular","v":"1.610891","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"tissue::stomach","v":"1.70025","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"tissue::bone marrow","v":"0.637308","d":"double"},{"po":110193,"n":"compartment::endosome","v":"5.